<section class="subhero wrap" aria-labelledby="page-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE PERSON BEHIND THE WORK</p><h1 id="page-title">Founder-led work.<br /><em>Shared understanding.</em></h1><p class="subhero-lede">I'm Nathan Grey, principal engineer at Studio Ember. I work with teams to clarify difficult platform decisions, build what is justified, and leave the knowledge with the people who own the result.</p><div class="action-row"><a class="button" href="{{ landing.bookingUrl }}" data-booking>Book a discovery call <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="{{ 'General question' | contactHref(page.url) }}">Email a general question <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><aside class="principal-card" aria-label="Nathan Grey, Principal Engineer"><span class="principal-monogram" aria-hidden="true">NG<span>✳</span></span><span class="eyebrow">NATHAN GREY / PRINCIPAL ENGINEER</span></aside></section>

<section class="section journey-section" aria-labelledby="about-approach-title"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">HOW I APPROACH THE WORK</p><h2 id="about-approach-title">Start with the people.<br /><em>Stay close to the problem.</em></h2></div></div><div class="offer-grid"><article><span class="eyebrow">01 / ASK</span><h3>Understand first.</h3><p>Learn what has changed, what the team needs to accomplish, and who will be responsible when the project ends.</p></article><article><span class="eyebrow">02 / CHOOSE</span><h3>Be deliberate.</h3><p>Use cloud-native practices where they help. Prefer a simpler architecture when it meets the need with less burden.</p></article><article><span class="eyebrow">03 / SHARE</span><h3>Make ownership practical.</h3><p>Work with the receiving team through documentation, validation, and instruction rather than leaving a system only its builder understands.</p></article></div></div></section>

